&z\ge\sum_{i=0}^{r-1}\sum_{c\in\mathcal L}(h-c)x_{i,c},\\
&\sum_{c\in\mathcal L}x_{i,c}\le B_i,\qquad x_{i,c}\ge0.
\end{aligned}
\]
This LP is not yet accepted as the full \(D_n\) reduction. It is, however, a useful candidate and already refutes any naive unequal-low "last low only" closed form inside the reduced model: the two-low path \(0,0.4,0.9,1\) has reduced-LP value \(68/225\), larger than the last-low value \(0.18\).

