./logs/iter_017_idea_02_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:2022:Iteration 15 adds a sharper two-level local regression test, CL-044, and refutes the proposed \(Q_T\)-based dichotomy via CL-046. The revised positive target is a resolved-surplus or debt recursion: low-horizon surplus \(S\) should matter only relative to the prefix length at the high that resolves it, and low-level quote mass creates persistent high debt that must be controlled cumulatively across droughts. This remains unproved, especially with multiple lows in one drought or overlapping drought intervals.
./logs/iter_017_idea_02_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:2024:Iteration 16 promotes the post-low single-drought extension CL-047: post-low zeros do not add local conflict beyond the resolving high debt. This strengthens the evidence that simple dilution is exact for one drought. The remaining gluing target shifts to multiple lows, unequal lows, and repeated droughts, where front-loading constraints and shared high debt may interact.
