./logs/iter_014_idea_02_explorer_01.stderr.log:1964:- Accepted the finite two-continuation lower bound: for \(0^N c\), \(c\in\{1/2,1\}\), every randomized learner has regret at least \(N/4\) on one continuation, using `sup` comparator or an epsilon-comparator variant.
